  "articleHtml": "<main>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head Burritos is built around customization, so there is no single calorie number that accurately describes every burrito or bowl.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Your entr\u00e9e style, tortilla, protein, rice, beans, cheese, vegetables, salsa, queso, guacamole, and finishing sauces all contribute to the final nutrition.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Use the\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Hot Head Burritos Nutrition Calculator above\n    </span>\n<span>\n     to recreate your order and see the combined calories, protein, carbohydrates, fat, sodium, fiber, and other available nutrition values.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.f2hc563zodbc\">\n<span>\n     Choose the Meal Style Before the Ingredients\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head Burritos currently lets you start with several different formats:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Burrito or Li\u2019l Burrito\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Bowl or Li\u2019l Bowl\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Taco\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Quesadilla\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Nachos\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The choice matters before a single filling is added.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A burrito introduces a flour tortilla. Nachos start with tortilla chips and queso. A quesadilla includes a tortilla and cheese as central parts of the recipe. A bowl removes the tortilla but still allows the same calorie-dense proteins, rice, beans, queso, cheese, guacamole, and sauces.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That is why the calculator should begin with the actual entr\u00e9e format instead of applying one average calorie value to every Hot Head meal.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.im2ai0q7wm08\">\n<span>\n     A Li\u2019l Meal Uses Different Portions\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head offers smaller\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Li\u2019l Burrito and Li\u2019l Bowl\n    </span>\n<span>\n     options.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These should not simply be treated as regular entr\u00e9es with fewer calories typed into the database. Ingredient quantities can be smaller too.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver already distinguishes several regular and Li\u2019l protein portions. For example, the current database lists regular Chicken at approximately 111 calories and the Li\u2019l Chicken portion at about 56 calories.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     When building a smaller entr\u00e9e, use Li\u2019l portions where applicable instead of combining a Li\u2019l tortilla or bowl with regular-size ingredient values.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.cane274cwmj6\">\n<span>\n     Tortilla Choice Creates a Different Starting Point\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For burritos and tacos, the tortilla contributes calories and carbohydrates before the fillings are added.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Current NutritionSolver entries include approximately:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Flour Tortilla:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     292 calories\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cheddar Jalape\u00f1o Tortilla:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     301 calories\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Li\u2019l Flour Tortilla:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     220 calories\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Soft Flour Taco:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     140 calories\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Soft Corn Taco:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     30 calories\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The difference can be meaningful, particularly when comparing a burrito with a bowl or flour tacos with corn tacos.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Choose the exact tortilla rather than applying a generic burrito shell value.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.lotmbg6gi9dg\">\n<span>\n     Protein Changes Calories, Protein, Fat, and Sodium\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head's current public menu lists core proteins such as chicken, steak, carnitas, barbacoa, and taco meat.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Different proteins can produce very different macro profiles.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For example, NutritionSolver currently lists:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chicken:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     111 calories and 16g protein\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Steak:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     117 calories and 21g protein\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Barbacoa:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     150 calories and 16g protein\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Taco Meat:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     193 calories and 14g protein\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This shows why the highest-calorie protein is not necessarily the highest-protein option.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Compare protein together with calories, fat, and sodium rather than judging the meal only by the meat name.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.n05iv3hu1lz9\">\n<span>\n     Rice and Beans Build the Carbohydrate Base\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head lets customers add rice and beans independently.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Current menu choices include white rice, brown rice, black beans, and pinto beans.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver currently lists Brown Rice at about\n    </span>\n<span>\n     150 calories and 31g carbs\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , while White Rice is approximately\n    </span>\n<span>\n     199 calories and 38g carbs\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you order both rice and beans, include both.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you skip rice or double a serving, the finished burrito or bowl should reflect that choice rather than relying on a standard preset total.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.tp0em9zvor8\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head Is Especially Sauce-Driven\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Sauces are one of the most distinctive parts of the Hot Head menu.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Current choices span several flavor and heat levels, including Sweet Habanero, Teriyaki, BBQ, Ranch, Taco Sauce, Hot Head Sauce, Avocado Lime, Southwest Ranch, Jalape\u00f1o Ranch, Cholula, Smoky Tabasco, Mango Habanero, and Straight Habanero.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These sauces are not nutritionally interchangeable.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Creamy sauces can contribute considerably more calories and fat than lighter hot sauces or salsas.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For an accurate meal, add every sauce you actually use instead of assuming heat level has no effect on nutrition.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.dvkdveat401w\">\n<span>\n     Salsa and Sauce Are Not the Same Thing\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head also separates its salsas from richer finishing sauces.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Current salsas include:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Pico\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Corn\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Verde\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Roja\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Wild\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Salsa may contribute fewer calories than many creamy sauces, but it can still add carbs, sugar, and sodium.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you combine salsa with Ranch, Hot Head Sauce, or another finishing sauce, both belong in the meal calculation.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.rejua7swwrdi\">\n<span>\n     Queso Can Appear in Several Different Ways\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head currently features\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Queso Blanco\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , queso-topped burritos, nachos, Queso Con Carne, Spicy Queso, and Smothered Burritos.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That creates an important serving distinction.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A small queso portion inside an entr\u00e9e is not necessarily the same serving as a side of queso or the amount used to smother a burrito.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver should preserve the context:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Entr\u00e9e queso portion\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Side queso\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Smothered entr\u00e9e\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     rather than using one queso number everywhere.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.7gcw7j1cj9xa\">\n<span>\n     Craft Recipes Have Defined Ingredient Combinations\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For users who do not build from scratch, Hot Head currently offers Craft Recipes such as Sweet Habanero, Hawaiian, Teriyaki, Americano, Chicken Bacon Ranch, Southwest Ranch, Jalape\u00f1o Ranch, Cheetos Flamin\u2019 Hot, and Leroy\u2019s Spicy Chicken.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These are useful as complete starting recipes.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you order a Craft Recipe exactly as designed, select the full recipe.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you change the protein, remove cheese, replace the rice, add queso, or use extra sauce, ingredient-level calculation becomes more accurate than keeping the original Craft Recipe total.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.x9b0gldjxdl6\">\n<span>\n     Power Bowls Need Their Own Nutrition\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head's current Power Bowls are designed around larger protein portions and specific ingredient combinations.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The current official menu lists approximately:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chicken Power Bowl:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     860 calories and 54g protein\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Steak Power Bowl:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     960 calories and 68g protein\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Veggie Power Bowl:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     750 calories and 23g protein.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These meals should not be estimated from an ordinary bowl because they use their own recipes, including ingredients such as double protein, rice, beans, vegetables, sauces, guacamole, cheese, and Supergreens.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.hw65cco5kfik\">\n<span>\n     Keto and Paleo Bowls Are Specific Recipes\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head also publishes Keto and Paleo bowl combinations.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These labels describe specific ingredient choices rather than guaranteeing one universal calorie or macro target.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A Keto Bowl made with chicken is different from a Keto Bowl using barbacoa, while the Paleo steak and pork recipes use their own combinations of vegetables, salsa, guacamole, and protein.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Use the exact recipe instead of applying one general \u201cketo bowl\u201d value.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.dc85ocsbwp3v\">\n<span>\n     Nachos Start With Chips and Queso\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Nachos should not be calculated as a bowl with chips added at the end.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head describes its nachos as tortilla chips loaded with queso and customizable toppings.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That means chips and queso are central components of the entr\u00e9e.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     After that come protein, beans, salsa, cheese, vegetables, guacamole, sour cream, and other toppings.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Build nachos from the correct base so queso or chips are not accidentally omitted or counted twice.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.uh0j0ogczm3y\">\n<span>\n     Toppings Can Range From Nearly Zero to Substantial\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Current toppings include vegetables and herbs such as lettuce, cilantro, banana peppers, jalape\u00f1os, fajita vegetables, and pineapple, along with cheese, sour cream, and other richer additions.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For example, NutritionSolver currently lists pineapple at approximately\n    </span>\n<span>\n     24 calories and 6g carbs\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , while some vegetable toppings contribute only a few calories.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cheese and sour cream can change the total more significantly.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A good calculator should therefore allow all toppings to be selected rather than lumping them together as one generic \u201cvegetables\u201d value.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.5vvopb7ssotg\">\n<span>\n     Sides Need Their Own Serving Size\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The current Hot Head menu includes:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chips\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Salsa\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Queso\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Guacamole\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Loaded Potatoes\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cookies\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Killer Brownie\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Side of Rice\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These should be calculated separately from the entr\u00e9e.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Current official menu values list chips at approximately\n    </span>\n<span>\n     385 calories\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , Killer Brownie at\n    </span>\n<span>\n     420 calories\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , and side portions of queso and guacamole across different calorie ranges depending on size.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A burrito plus chips and queso is therefore a very different order from the burrito alone.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.nee3pyw94s86\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head Burritos Nutrition Questions\n    </span>\n</h2><div class=\"faq-accordion-container space-y-3 my-6\"><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How many calories are in a Hot Head Burrito?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Is a Hot Head bowl lower in calories than a burrito?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Does Hot Head have smaller portions?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Which Hot Head Power Bowl has the most protein?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Does Hot Head queso add calories?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How do I calculate a custom Hot Head meal?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details></div>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.g50x2wl961mz\">\n<span>\n     Build the Hot Head Meal You Actually Order\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hot Head Burritos is one of the restaurant menus where ingredient-level calculation makes the most sense.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Start with your\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Burrito, Li\u2019l Burrito, Bowl, Li\u2019l Bowl, Taco, Quesadilla, or Nachos\n    </span>\n<span>\n     . Then add the exact\n    </span>\n<span>\n     protein, rice, beans, salsa, toppings, queso, guacamole, and sauces\n    </span>\n<span>\n     you choose.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That gives you a far more useful nutrition estimate than assigning one fixed calorie number to every customized Hot Head Burrito.\n    </span>\n</p>\n</main>",
